        "thinking": "I'm trying to identify which root this form comes from — there seem to be multiple लुठ् roots with different meanings and पद classifications, so I need to figure out which one fits here.\n\nGoing through the kuṭādi gaṇa list in तुदादि, I'm confirming \"लुट संश्लेषणे\" is indeed the verb listed there, not \"लुठ\" — so I need to double-check which root and meaning actually applies to the word in question.\n\nI'm trying to pin down whether लुठ् belongs to कुटादि and how that affects its लुङ् form — whether it would be अलुठिष्म or अलोठिष्म, weighing whether सेट् guna applies or is blocked by the कुटादि ङित्वत् treatment.\n\nI'm also checking alternative roots: a भ्वादि लुठ् (परस्मैपदी, लोठति) doesn't fit since its लङ् would be अलोठाम्, and a द्युतादि रुट्/लुट्/लुठ् meaning \"प्रतिघाते\" is आत्मनेपदी with लोठते, which also doesn't match — so I'm settling back on the तुदादि लुठ् as the right one.\n\nNow I'm trying to confirm whether this root belongs to the कुटादि group by recalling the Madhaviya Dhatuvrtti listing, which enumerates roots like कुट, पुट, कुच, गुज, गुड, डिप, छुर, स्फुट, मुट, त्रुट, तुट, चुट, छुट, जुड — but I don't see लुठ् explicitly named there yet.\n\nI recall that since लुठ् belongs to kutadi gaṇa, it takes luṅ with the iṭ augment, giving अलुठिष्म rather than अलोठिष्म. I'll settle on अलुठिष्म as my answer.\n\n",
